Third-party Fabric artifacts, vendored as a regression corpus
==========================================================

78 real Microsoft Fabric exports collected from 17 public GitHub
repositories: 14 corpus, 25 notebooks, 30 pipelines, 9 warehouse.

WHY THESE AND NOT MORE
----------------------
The set they were drawn from has 149 files from 42 repositories. Only the
78 whose source repository carries a permissive licence are here.
The other 71 are deliberately absent:

  59  no licence at all -- all rights reserved, so redistribution is not ours
      to grant
   2  GPL-2.0 -- copyleft, and it would conflict with this repository's MIT
      licence
  10  a licence GitHub cannot identify, which is not the same as permission

Licences represented: 77 x MIT, 1 x MPL-2.0

Every file's source repository, path, URL and licence is recorded in the
PROVENANCE.json beside it. Each remains under its own licence and its own
copyright holders; vendoring here is redistribution under those terms, not a
transfer of them. The copyright and permission notices those licences require
are reproduced in full in ../THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

WHY VENDOR THEM AT ALL
----------------------
A fixture written alongside the rules encodes the same misunderstanding as the
rules and cannot falsify them. These can, and have: they are why .ipynb support
exists, why the Synapse notebook header is accepted, why activities nested in a
ForEach are walked, and why pipeline-to-pipeline ordering edges are captured.

